---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility statement for the-manchesters.com."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
      <h1>The Manchesters Accessibility Statement</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        This accessibility statement applies to the website www.the-manchesters.com, operated by
        The Manchesters.
      </p>
      <p>
        We want as many people as possible to be able to use this website. For example, that
        means you should be able to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Zoom in up to 300% without the text spilling off the screen.</li>
        <li>Navigate most of the website using a keyboard or speech recognition software.</li>
        <li>
          Listen to most of the website using a screen reader (including recent versions of JAWS,
          NVDA, and VoiceOver).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We have also made the website text as simple as possible to understand.</p>

      <h2>How accessible this website is</h2>
      <p>
        We continuously monitor our website to ensure it remains accessible to all users.
        However, we know some parts of this website may not be fully accessible:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Some media clips or downloadable PDFs may not yet be fully tagged for screen readers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Feedback and contact information</h2>
      <p>
        If you need information on this website in a different format — such as an accessible
        PDF, large print, easy read, audio recording, or braille — please contact us:
      </p>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:bookings@the-manchesters.com">bookings@the-manchesters.com</a></p>
      <p>We will consider your request and get back to you within 7 working days.</p>

      <h2>Reporting accessibility problems with this website</h2>
      <p>
        We are always looking to improve the accessibility of this website. If you find any
        problems not listed on this page or think we are not meeting accessibility requirements,
        please contact us:
      </p>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:bookings@the-manchesters.com">bookings@the-manchesters.com</a></p>

      <h2>Enforcement procedure</h2>
      <p>
        The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the Equality
        Act 2010 (the 'equality duty') in Great Britain.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have reported an accessibility issue to us and are not happy with how we respond,
        you can contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS) for advice and support:
      </p>
      <p>Website: www.equalityadvisoryservice.com</p>
      <p>Phone: 0808 800 0082</p>

      <h2>Technical information about this website's accessibility</h2>
      <p>
        The Manchesters is committed to making its website accessible, in accordance with the
        Equality Act 2010.
      </p>

      <h3>Compliance status</h3>
      <p>
        This website is partially compliant with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)
        version 2.2 AA standard.
      </p>

      <h3>How we tested this website</h3>
      <p>
        This website was last tested on 10 September 2026. The test was carried out by The Manchesters using
        automated testing tools alongside manual keyboard and screen reader checks.
      </p>
      <p>We tested a sample of key pages including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Home page (/)</li>
        <li>Main content and media pages</li>
        <li>Contact and enquiry pages (/contact)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Preparation of this accessibility statement</h3>
      <p>This statement was prepared on 10 September 2026. It was last reviewed on 10 September 2026.</p>

      <p>
        In the meantime, if anything on this site is difficult to use, please email
        <a href="mailto:bookings@the-manchesters.com">bookings@the-manchesters.com</a> and we'll do
        our best to help.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
</style>
